"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and May to June came in under 90% of normal in 33 of them. In 2025, August to September came in at 48% of normal on the middle of the grids, and July to August at 54%. So far in 2026, May to June came in at 147% of normal and April to May at 144%. On grid 29331, the preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 is 68.6, a NOAA number and not the final RMA index.</p>"}
